# Day 48

## Experiment Title

Creating and Managing Jenkins Freestyle Projects


## Objective

To understand how freestyle projects are created and managed in Jenkins.


## Theory

Freestyle projects are one of the basic project types available in Jenkins. They allow users to configure and automate build tasks through a graphical interface without requiring complex pipeline scripts.

Freestyle projects support source code management, build triggers, build steps, and post build actions. They are commonly used for simple Continuous Integration tasks and automation processes.


## Requirements

Jenkins

Java Development Kit

Docker Desktop

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Jenkins dashboard through the web browser.

Create a new freestyle project in Jenkins.

Configure project details and build settings.

Add source code management and build steps.

Save the project configuration.

Execute the build process and observe the build status.


## Output

The Jenkins freestyle project was created successfully.

Build execution completed successfully in Jenkins.

Project configuration and build details were displayed correctly.


## Result

Successfully created and managed freestyle projects in Jenkins.
